ruyiseek (0.1.0-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Right-click context menu on result rows. Slint 1.6 does not expose
    PopupMenu / MenuItem / MouseArea (they are not part of
    std-widgets.slint and only MouseArea-like surface is the
    PointerEventButton enum used internally by TouchArea's
    pointer-event), so the menu is hand-rolled: each menu item is a
    Rectangle + TouchArea pair, the wrapper is a Rectangle positioned
    by popup-index so it lines up with the row that was clicked,
    and right-button up events on a result row set popup-index +
    selected-index without triggering the normal activate callback.
  * Four actions:
      - 打开           re-uses the existing activate handler (xdg-open);
      - 打开所在文件夹  reveals the parent directory in the user's
                       default file manager via xdg-open on
                       path.parent() (fallback "/" when parent is
                       empty). The reveal_parent helper is unit-tested.
      - 复制文件       puts file://<abs path> onto the clipboard as
                       text/uri-list so file managers can paste it.
                       Picks xclip on X11, wl-copy on Wayland, and
                       falls back to the other tool if the preferred
                       one is missing.
      - 复制路径       puts the absolute path string onto the clipboard
                       as plain text. Same xclip / wl-copy selection
                       and fallback logic.
    All copy operations report success or failure in the launcher's
    status bar so the user gets immediate feedback instead of a silent
    no-op when neither clipboard tool is installed.
  * Dismissal: clicking a result row, clicking a menu item, or editing
    the search input all reset popup-index to -1. Entering settings
    mode also resets popup-index and the menu Rectangle additionally
    binds its visible to !settings-mode so it cannot leak through the
    panel.
  * Bug fix: re-summoning the launcher (double-Ctrl, tray Show,
    --toggle) now clears the previous query and result list, so the
    second invocation always starts on an empty input. The reset
    happens in show_launcher: if query is non-empty, set_query("")
    triggers on_query_edited which already clears results, bumps
    the search-response generation, and zeroes selected-index; if
    query is already empty, selected-index is reset directly so a
    stale selection cannot survive across toggles.
  * Packaging: Suggests adds xclip and wl-clipboard so users who want
    the copy actions get a one-line `apt install xclip` suggestion
    without it being pulled in by default.

 -- RuyiSeek contributors <ruyiseek@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 23:40:00 +0000

ruyiseek (0.1.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * UI: closing the settings window now returns to the launcher instead of
    hiding the entire window. Previously the close button called
    launcher.hide() and dropped the visible flag, which forced the user
    to either re-press Ctrl twice or click the tray to bring the
    launcher back; now the handler exits settings mode, focuses the
    search input, and re-marks the window visible so the user can keep
    typing immediately. Escape / tray Hide / double-Ctrl still act as
    full-hide shortcuts.
  * ruyiseekd: when started with no --root (the path taken by
    ruyiseek-ui's detached fork in ensure_daemon_running), fall back to
    $HOME first instead of current_dir. Without this, a daemon forked
    from a process with cwd=/ would fill the snapshot with kernel
    modules and glibc paths and starve the user's real files out of
    the Top-K. $HOME fallback is verified by a new unit test
    no_root_arg_falls_back_to_home_when_available.
  * Build: move packaging/deb/shim.c to packaging/shim.c so the source
    stays out of the .deb, and have packaging/deb/build.sh compile it
    into packaging/deb/shim.o before every musl cargo invocation.
    Previously shim.c lived at the top of the .deb staging tree and
    was deleted by build.sh's cleanup find, breaking the next clean
    build with "cannot open shim.o".
  * Documentation: align implementation-status.md, README.md, and the
    long-form design doc with the actual 0.1.0-6/7 source layout.
    implementation-status moves A1.5 to "已完成" and adds an A1.6
    follow-up section. README adds an "安装包（DEB）" section and the
    .deb / auto-fork / arrow-nav bullet points. The design doc drops
    the never-implemented integration-host prose (sections 6.1, 6.2),
    lists only the 5 crates + 3 apps that actually exist, fixes the
    systemd units in 18.4 to Type=simple with Requires=ruyiseekd,
    prunes CLI subcommands in 20.3 to the four that are implemented,
    and updates the install path table in 25.2 to the files produced
    by packaging/deb/build.sh.

