ruyiseek (0.1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the arrow-key navigation bug reported as "无法用方向键选择文件".
    Slint 1.6 routes KeyEvent through process_key_input in
    child-before-parent order, and the focused LineEdit's internal
    TextInput is the focus_item (declared via forward-focus); it accepts
    Up/Down/Left/Right to move its own text cursor and returns
    EventAccepted, which terminates the focus walk before any
    user-defined key-pressed handler on a parent FocusScope can see
    the event. As a result, no amount of slint-side handler placement
    can intercept the arrow keys while the input still owns focus.
  * Resolve by handling arrows at the XInput2 layer. The platform
    crate's hotkey worker now classifies Up/Down/Left/Right keysyms
    from the raw keycode->keysym map and dispatches them through a new
    on_arrow callback. ruyiseek-ui forwards the callback through the
    UI event channel as UiEvent::Arrow; the pump only acts on it when
    the launcher window is visible, so arrow keys in other apps are
    ignored.
  * apply_arrow_to_selection adjusts the launcher's selected-index
    by ±1 (Up decreases, Down increases), clamped to [0, len-1].
    PageUp/PageDown (jump 5), Ctrl+P/N (prev/next), Ctrl+L (clear
    query), and Escape (clear/dismiss) remain slint-side and continue
    to work because the LineEdit does not consume them.
  * No user-visible side effects when the launcher is hidden: the
    callback fires but apply_arrow_to_selection early-returns because
    the visibility guard fails.

