ruyiseek (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update the post-install banner so it reflects the new auto-start
    behavior. The previous message told users to run
    `systemctl --user enable --now ruyiseekd.service` (or log out and
    back in) before the launcher would work; that is no longer required
    because ruyiseek-ui now spawns the daemon itself. The new message
    describes the install-and-click flow, lists the common subcommands
    (--settings, --background, --quit), and demotes the systemd user
    units to an optional "log in and the tray starts automatically"
    follow-up rather than a prerequisite.
  * No binary changes; this is a documentation-only release.

 -- RuyiSeek contributors <ruyiseek@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 16:09:00 +0000

ruyiseek (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the UI binary auto-start the ruyiseekd daemon if it is not
    already running. Previously a fresh install (or a daemon that was
    killed) would surface "无法连接后台服务：..." in the status bar
    because the launcher's Exec= /usr/bin/ruyiseek-ui only started the
    UI, never the daemon. Now ruyiseek-ui probes the socket on startup
    and, if it is unreachable, spawns the sibling ruyiseekd binary,
    waits up to 5 s for it to bind, then proceeds. The daemon is
    forked as a detached child (its std::process::Child handle is
    dropped so the OS reparents it to PID 1 when the UI exits), so
    closing the UI no longer takes the indexer down with it.
  * Install flow: install .deb → click launcher → daemon and UI both
    come up with no extra steps. Users who already manage ruyiseekd
    via systemd --user see no change (the probe returns early).
  * Best-effort: any failure to start the daemon is logged to stderr
    but does not abort the UI; the existing "无法连接后台服务" status
    bar message is still shown in that case.

 -- RuyiSeek contributors <ruyiseek@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 15:35:00 +0000

ruyiseek (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Revert the fully-static musl build for ruyiseek-ui. Musl's libc.a
    ships a stub dlopen that returns "Dynamic loading not supported"
    without issuing any syscall, so x11-dl (and therefore winit's X11
    backend) cannot load libX11.so.6 at runtime on a fully static
    binary. Verified by strace showing zero openat() calls for any .so
    on a musl-static build and by disassembling dlopen.lo in
    libc.a (weak_alias(stub_dlopen, dlopen)).
  * Switch to a hybrid build: ruyi-cli and ruyiseekd are now built for
    x86_64-unknown-linux-musl (no C runtime deps), while ruyiseek-ui
    is built for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu so glibc's real dlopen
    resolves libX11.so.6 via ldconfig on the host.
  * Drop Depends: libgcc-s1 -- the UOS 20 / DDE apt repo renames it
    back to libgcc1 (libgcc-s1 has no candidate). Both names provide
    the same libgcc_s.so.1 file at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/.
  * Final Depends: libc6, libgcc1, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxi6,
    libxcursor1, libx11-xcb1, libxkbcommon0, libfontconfig1 -- all
    standard GUI stack packages pulled in on any UOS / Debian desktop.

 -- RuyiSeek contributors <ruyiseek@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 13:10:00 +0000

ruyiseek (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Switch release binaries from x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu to
    x86_64-unknown-linux-musl. The three binaries (ruyi, ruyiseekd,
    ruyiseek-ui) are now fully statically linked — no libc6,
    libgcc-s1, libpthread, libm, libdl, or librt runtime
    dependencies. The Depends line drops to libx11-6 only,
    matching the requirements of UOS 20 / Debian 10 hosts where
    libgcc-s1 cannot be installed.
  * Link with rust-lld (the bundled LLD inside the Rust toolchain)
    instead of the system GNU ld. rust-lld correctly handles the
    rust runtime's _start auxiliary-vector relocation that system
    ld was collapsing to address 0 (causing startup segfaults).
  * Add packaging/deb/shim.c defining __dlopen/__dlclose/__dlerror
    as weak stubs to satisfy any residual glibc libdl.a references
    when cc-rs compiles vendored C dependencies.
  * Update build.sh to also exclude shim.c / shim.o from the
    binary .deb package (they are build-time only).

